// The DSP3210's boot ROM: the silicon's first 112 words (WinUAE
// dsp3210/DSP3210_emulation.cpp, DSP_onboard_ROM; the manual's Listing A-1 is an
// earlier revision of the same code), the rest of the 256 words filled with each
// word's own address in Processor mode (0x50030000 + offset), as Listing A-1 fills it.
function automatic [31:0] dsp_rom(input [7:0] a);
